{
    "background_story": "Saoirse was a rugged and dependable dockworker in the bustling port city of Dublin. Her colleagues affectionately called her 'The Lumper' due to her exceptional strength and agility in loading and unloading cargo from the ships. Saoirse took pride in her work, ensuring that every crate and barrel was handled with care and precision. Her broad shoulders and quick reflexes made her a valuable asset to the dock team, earning her a reputation as one of the toughest and most reliable lumpers on the waterfront. Despite the physically demanding nature of her job, Saoirse's warm smile and kind heart made her a beloved figure among the sailors and merchants who passed through the port.",
